-- Antitrust Guidelines for International Enforcement and Cooperation (DOJ/FTC, 13 January 2017):
-- INDEPENDENT TESTS.
--
-- The expected answers were written from the source text alone, before this encoding was
-- opened, and frozen (sha256 1d2a3c6f197d75493e3a9a9f667cb155bfa5a86df56f60ca72bceb8f6053aa40 of
-- the test author's answers.md, 2026-11-25T18:15Z). Each group names the answer it asserts (A6,
-- N4b, CP5 ...). An assertion that fails is a finding and is left failing.
--
-- What was read of the encoding, all of it after the freeze: the six modules in full (nouns and
-- the five rule modules, bodies and fork comments included); check.sh; and lines 1-75 of
-- intl-tests.l4, read for the IMPORT and record-construction syntax, which hold that file's
-- Example A fixture and three of its assertions (the two Example A records and three Example A
-- assertions below coincide with them). NOTES.md's fork register was read only after both builds
-- had run this file. The eight failing assertions were predicted from the rule bodies and marked
-- "expected to FAIL" before the first run; the one assertion added after a run is marked so.
--
-- Where an answer "accepts either" two values, the assertion is an OR of the two. Where the
-- frozen answer says the text gives an answer for which the encoding has no value (it returns
-- NOTHING), the assertion is "not NOTHING and not the wrong value", which cannot hold: that is
-- the finding, stated in the comment.
--
-- Pages are pdf pages of the 55-page PDF (printed page + 3). Target dialect: main.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Builders`

-- An effect on U.S. commerce, positional: the commerce, then the five findings in the order of
-- the record (proximate cause, substantial, foreseeable, adverse, proximately caused the
-- claimant's injury). NOTHING is "not yet found".
GIVEN ce IS A `Commerce an effect is on (3.2)`
      px IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      sb IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      fs IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      ad IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      ij IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce (3.2)`
`ind effect` ce px sb fs ad ij MEANS `Effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce (3.2)` WITH
    `the commerce affected` IS ce
    `the effect is proximately caused by the conduct` IS px
    `the effect is substantial` IS sb
    `the effect is foreseeable to a reasonable person making practical business judgments` IS fs
    `the effect is an adverse one` IS ad
    `the effect proximately caused the claimant's injury` IS ij

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim (3.2)`
      xb IS A BOOLEAN
      fi IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claim (3.2)`
`ind claim` k xb fi MEANS `Claim (3.2)` WITH
    `the kind of claim` IS k
    `the claim is for injury to export business in the United States` IS xb
    `the claimant's injury is a foreign injury` IS fi

`ind criminal` MEANS `ind claim` `a criminal enforcement action brought by the Department` FALSE FALSE
`ind equitable` MEANS `ind claim` `a civil action for equitable relief brought by the agencies` FALSE FALSE
`ind private` MEANS `ind claim` `a damages action brought by a private plaintiff` FALSE FALSE
`ind private, foreign injury` MEANS `ind claim` `a damages action brought by a private plaintiff` FALSE TRUE
`ind 4A` MEANS `ind claim` `a damages action by the United States under Section 4A of the Clayton Act` FALSE FALSE
`ind criminal, export business` MEANS `ind claim` `a criminal enforcement action brought by the Department` TRUE FALSE
`ind private, export business` MEANS `ind claim` `a damages action brought by a private plaintiff` TRUE FALSE

-- Effects used below.
`ind import, DSRF` MEANS `ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING
`ind domestic, DSRF` MEANS `ind effect` `trade or commerce within the United States` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING
`ind export, DSRF` MEANS `ind effect` `the export trade or commerce of a person engaged in such trade or commerce in the United States` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `Commerce facts (built by me; the record fields are the encoding's)`

-- Example A (3.1, pdf 23): Corps 1 and 2 in Alpha fix Widget X prices, sell worldwide incl. in
-- or for delivery to the US; worldwide agreement; I also set "small portion" TRUE (A's last
-- sentence) in a second record.
`ind Example A` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS TRUE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS FALSE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

`ind Example A, small share` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS TRUE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS TRUE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

-- Example B (pdf 23-24), first limb: shipping services closely connected to importation.
`ind Example B` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS FALSE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS TRUE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS FALSE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

-- I2 (3.1, pdf 22): the participants are importers, but the challenged conduct (here a cartel
-- on sales in a third country) does not itself involve import commerce. I set "involves export
-- commerce" FALSE, so the non-import kind is wholly foreign.
`ind importers, conduct not import` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS FALSE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS TRUE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS FALSE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

-- I3 (3.1, pdf 22): a firm that outsources delivery to the US. It is not the importer, but
-- its product is sold for delivery to the US.
`ind outsourced delivery` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS TRUE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS TRUE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

-- Examples C and D (pdf 25-28): wholly foreign commerce. Corps 1 and 2 do not sell in or for
-- delivery to the US.
`ind wholly foreign` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS FALSE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS FALSE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS FALSE

-- C3 (n.80, pdf 20): some of the challenged conduct takes place in the US.
`ind partly in US` MEANS `Facts of the commerce the conduct involves (3)` WITH
    `the conduct involves trade or commerce with foreign nations` IS TRUE
    `the participants sell the goods or services concerned in or for delivery to the United States` IS FALSE
    `the conduct concerns services closely connected to the importation of goods into the United States` IS FALSE
    `the agencies find that the challenged conduct otherwise itself involves U.S. import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants are also engaged in import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the participants themselves act as importers` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is directed specifically or exclusively at import commerce` IS FALSE
    `the import commerce involved is a relatively small portion of the worldwide commerce involved` IS FALSE
    `the conduct involves U.S. export commerce` IS FALSE
    `some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States` IS TRUE

§§ `A. Chapter 2 tests (pdf 7-19)`

-- A1, A2 (2, pdf 7): nationality changes nothing; both determinations give "same substantive
-- rules". Nexus missing: my answer says text silent here, so NOTHING is accepted.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
      nx IS A BOOLEAN
      cm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determinations before the same substantive rules apply (2)`
`ind determinations` n nx cm MEANS `Determinations before the same substantive rules apply (2)` WITH
    `the agencies determine that a sufficient nexus to the United States exists to apply the antitrust laws` IS nx
    `the agencies determine that neither international comity nor the involvement of a foreign jurisdiction precludes investigation or enforcement` IS cm
    `the nationality of the parties` IS n

#ASSERT `2: the substantive rules the agencies apply` (`ind determinations` "United States" TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies apply the same substantive rules to all cases, and do not discriminate based on the nationality of the parties`
#ASSERT `2: the substantive rules the agencies apply` (`ind determinations` "United States" TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `2: the substantive rules the agencies apply` (`ind determinations` "Country Alpha" TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `2: the substantive rules the agencies apply` (`ind determinations` "Country Alpha" FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- A3 last line (2.4, pdf 11): a transaction not subject to HSR, a statute applies: the
-- agencies "may seek to block or undo".
#ASSERT `2.4: what the agencies may seek against a transaction` (`Transaction and the HSR Act (2.4)` WITH `the transaction is subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements` IS FALSE, `the Sherman Act, the FTC Act or the Clayton Act applies to the transaction` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST `though the transaction is not subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements, the agencies may seek to block or undo an anticompetitive merger or acquisition, or seek other equitable relief`

-- A6 (2.7, pdf 14-15): NCRPA.
GIVEN nt IS A BOOLEAN
      sc IS A BOOLEAN
      jp IS A BOOLEAN
      fa IS A BOOLEAN
      cp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notified venture under the NCRPA (2.7)`
`ind venture` nt sc jp fa cp MEANS `Notified venture under the NCRPA (2.7)` WITH
    `the participants have provided notice to the agencies under the procedure` IS nt
    `the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification` IS sc
    `the venture is a joint production venture` IS jp
    `the principal facilities for such production are located in the United States or its territories` IS fa
    `each person who controls any party to the venture, the party included, is a United States person, or a foreign person from a country whose law accords antitrust treatment no less favorable to United States persons than to its domestic persons for participation in joint ventures for production` IS cp

-- notified, within scope, not a production venture: actual damages only.
#ASSERT `2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, monetary relief in a private civil suit is limited to actual, rather than treble, damages`
-- notified, outside scope: limitation not available.
#ASSERT `2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the limit to actual damages applies only so long as the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification`
-- joint production venture, both conditions: limited.
#ASSERT `2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, monetary relief in a private civil suit is limited to actual, rather than treble, damages`
-- joint production venture, facilities abroad: not available.
#ASSERT `2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the benefit is not available to the joint production venture`
-- joint production venture, a controlling person from a less favourable country: not available.
#ASSERT `2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the benefit is not available to the joint production venture`
-- A6, not notified: my frozen answer is "limitation not available" (the text's "if participants
-- provide notice"). The encoding has no value for that and returns NOTHING (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT (NOT (`2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING)) AND (NOT (`2.7: damages against a notified venture` (`ind venture` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, monetary relief in a private civil suit is limited to actual, rather than treble, damages`))

-- A7 (2.8, pdf 15): Webb-Pomerene.
GIVEN gd IS A BOOLEAN
      ae IS A BOOLEAN
      dc IS A BOOLEAN
      fl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Export association (2.8)`
`ind association` gd ae dc fl MEANS `Export association (2.8)` WITH
    `it is an association of otherwise competing businesses engaging collectively in export sales` IS TRUE
    `the exports are of goods, wares, or merchandise` IS gd
    `the conduct has an anticompetitive effect in the United States` IS ae
    `the conduct injures domestic competitors of the members of the association` IS dc
    `the association files its articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission` IS fl

-- export of services: not exempt.
#ASSERT `2.8: the Webb-Pomerene exemption` (`ind association` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `outside the exemption, by a limit the 2017 text states`
#ASSERT elem `the exemption applies only to the export of goods, wares, or merchandise` (`2.8: the limits of the exemption that the association meets` (`ind association` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- anticompetitive effect in the US: not exempt.
#ASSERT `2.8: the Webb-Pomerene exemption` (`ind association` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `outside the exemption, by a limit the 2017 text states`
-- injures domestic competitors: not exempt.
#ASSERT `2.8: the Webb-Pomerene exemption` (`ind association` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `outside the exemption, by a limit the 2017 text states`
-- goods, no US effect, no injury, files: within, and no foreign immunity.
#ASSERT `2.8: the Webb-Pomerene exemption` (`ind association` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `within the limited antitrust exemption as the 2017 text describes it, which provides no immunity from prosecution under foreign antitrust laws`

-- A8 (2.9, pdf 16-17): ETCR.
GIVEN s1 IS A BOOLEAN
      s2 IS A BOOLEAN
      s3 IS A BOOLEAN
      s4 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Showing by an applicant for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
`ind showing` s1 s2 s3 s4 MEANS `Showing by an applicant for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)` WITH
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will result in neither a substantial lessening of competition or restraint of trade within the United States nor a substantial restraint of the export trade of any competitor of the applicant` IS s1
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not unreasonably enhance, stabilize, or depress prices in the United States of the class of goods or services covered by the application` IS s2
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not constitute unfair methods of competition against competitors engaged in the export of the class of goods or services exported by the applicant` IS s3
    `the applicant shows that the conduct will not include any act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services` IS s4

-- one standard (the fourth) not shown: it is listed, so the applicant cannot obtain one.
#ASSERT `2.9: the standards the applicant has not shown` (`ind showing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `no act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services`
#ASSERT null (`2.9: the standards the applicant has not shown` (`ind showing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

GIVEN nm IS A BOOLEAN
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
      co IS A BOOLEAN
      fr IS A BOOLEAN
      rv IS A BOOLEAN
      hm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Conduct under an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
`ind certified` nm sp co fr rv hm MEANS `Conduct under an export trade certificate of review (2.9)` WITH
    `the person is named in the certificate` IS nm
    `the activity is specified in the certificate` IS sp
    `the activity complies with the terms of the certificate` IS co
    `the certificate was obtained by fraud` IS fr
    `the Secretary of Commerce or the Department determines that the export activities have ceased to comply with the statutory criteria` IS rv
    `the conduct threatens a clear and irreparable harm to the national interest` IS hm

#ASSERT `2.9: conduct under a certificate` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the certificate is void from the outset, and offers no protection under the antitrust laws`
#ASSERT `2.9: conduct under a certificate` (`ind certified` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the conduct falls outside the scope of the certificate, and remains fully subject to private and governmental enforcement actions`
#ASSERT `2.9: conduct under a certificate` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `limited immunity from suit under both federal and state antitrust laws, within the limits section 2.9 states`
#ASSERT elem `the certificate does not insulate the conduct from investigation or enforcement by a foreign antitrust authority` (`2.9: the limits that remain on the certified conduct` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT elem `a person injured by certified conduct may recover actual, though not treble, damages if the conduct is found to violate any of the statutory criteria, and in such an action certified conduct enjoys a presumption of legality` (`2.9: the limits that remain on the certified conduct` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT elem `the Department may bring suit under Section 15 of the Clayton Act to enjoin the conduct, even if it has been pre-approved as part of the certificate` (`2.9: the limits that remain on the certified conduct` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT elem `the Secretary of Commerce may revoke or modify the certificate` (`2.9: the limits that remain on the certified conduct` (`ind certified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))

-- A9 (2.12, pdf 19): trade-dispute settlements.
GIVEN cp IS A BOOLEAN
      bd IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Settlement of a trade dispute (2.12)`
`ind settlement` cp bd MEANS `Settlement of a trade dispute (2.12)` WITH
    `the agreement complies with the specific procedures in the U.S. trade laws` IS cp
    `the agreement goes beyond the measures authorized by such laws` IS bd
    `the settlement involves price and quantity agreements or otherwise implicates the antitrust laws` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `2.12: a trade-dispute settlement` (`ind settlement` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agreement is subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute`
#ASSERT `2.12: a trade-dispute settlement` (`ind settlement` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agreement is subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute`
-- A9, complying settlement within the authorised measures, with price and quantity terms: my
-- frozen answer is "implied immunity". The encoding has no value for it and returns NOTHING
-- (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT (NOT (`2.12: a trade-dispute settlement` (`ind settlement` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING)) AND (NOT (`2.12: a trade-dispute settlement` (`ind settlement` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agreement is subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute`))
-- officials involved, no legal authority: does not immunize.
#ASSERT `2.12: officials' involvement in the measures` (`Government officials and the measures (2.12)` WITH `there is legal authority for the measures` IS FALSE, `U.S. or foreign government officials were involved in or encouraged the measures` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the officials' involvement or encouragement, without more, does not immunize the arrangement`

§§ `B. Chapter 3 opening (pdf 19-21)`

-- C5, C6 (3, pdf 21).
#ASSERT `3: how the FTAIA bears on` `the Clayton Act` EQUALS `the FTAIA did not address the reach of the Clayton Act, but the agencies would apply the principles of chapter 3 when making enforcement decisions on mergers and acquisitions involving trade or commerce with foreign nations`
#ASSERT `3: how the FTAIA bears on` `the FTC Act` EQUALS `Section 5(a)(3) of the FTC Act, added by the FTAIA, closely parallels Section 6a of the Sherman Act`

-- C1 (3, pdf 19-20): sufficient connection, a hedged "generally will proceed ... subject to
-- chapter 4". Import conduct (Example A), the Department's criminal action, no effects findings.
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind Example A` EMPTY `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `a circumstance chapter 3 describes as a sufficient connection: if the agencies so determine, they generally will proceed in the normal course, subject to the considerations of chapter 4 and principles of prosecutorial discretion`
-- C2 (n.82, pdf 21): FTAIA precludes the claim: "will not proceed". Wholly foreign conduct,
-- one effect found not substantial.
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind equitable` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not proceed: the FTAIA precludes the claim on the merits or strips the court of jurisdiction, and courts of appeals differ on which without affecting the agencies' decision`
-- C3 (n.80, pdf 20).
#ASSERT `n.80: the showing of a substantial and intended effect` `ind partly in US` EMPTY EQUALS JUST `in the agencies' view, a separate showing of substantial and intended effects is unnecessary, because some of the challenged conduct takes place in the United States`

§§ `C. Section 3.1 import commerce (pdf 22-24)`

-- I1 and Example A (pdf 22-23): import commerce, general requirements, s.6a does not exempt.
#ASSERT `3: the commerce the conduct involves` `ind Example A` EQUALS `U.S. import commerce`
#ASSERT `3: what the FTAIA does with the conduct` `ind Example A` EQUALS `the conduct is subject to the general requirements of the Sherman Act or the FTC Act for effects on commerce, not to the special requirements spelled out in the FTAIA`
-- I4 and Example A's last sentence: a small share does not change it.
#ASSERT `3: the commerce the conduct involves` `ind Example A, small share` EQUALS `U.S. import commerce`
-- I2: participants are importers, conduct not import: exclusion does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`3.1: the challenged conduct itself involves U.S. import commerce` `ind importers, conduct not import`)
#ASSERT `3: what the FTAIA does with the conduct` `ind importers, conduct not import` EQUALS `the FTAIA initially places the conduct outside the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act, unless its effects exception brings it back`
-- I3: outsourcing delivery does not escape the exclusion.
#ASSERT `3.1: the challenged conduct itself involves U.S. import commerce` `ind outsourced delivery`
-- Example B (pdf 23-24): shipping services closely connected to importation are import commerce.
#ASSERT `3: the commerce the conduct involves` `ind Example B` EQUALS `U.S. import commerce`
-- Example B, hedged effects ("likely"): with no finding, the effects test is not answered.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect is direct, substantial, and reasonably foreseeable` (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `D. Section 3.2 non-import foreign commerce (pdf 21, 24-29)`

-- N1: wholly foreign conduct is initially outside the reach.
#ASSERT `3: what the FTAIA does with the conduct` `ind wholly foreign` EQUALS `the FTAIA initially places the conduct outside the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act, unless its effects exception brings it back`
-- N2a: all three found, sovereign claim: brought back.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST `ind import, DSRF`) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception brings the conduct back within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N2b, N2c, N2d: one requirement found false: not within reach.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N2e: DSRF found, but for a private damages claim the effect is found not to have caused the
-- plaintiff's injury: does not give rise, not within reach.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))) `ind private` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N2f: no effect on any US commerce (empty list): not within reach.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` EMPTY `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N4a: effect only on a US exporter's export commerce, claim for injury to export business: covered.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST `ind export, DSRF`) `ind criminal, export business` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception brings the conduct back within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N4b: same effect, claim not for export business: not covered.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST `ind export, DSRF`) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception is met only through the effect on export commerce, so the Acts apply only for injury to export business in the United States, which this claim is not for`
-- N4c: effects on domestic and export commerce: the export limit does not apply.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST `ind export, DSRF`, `ind domestic, DSRF`) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception brings the conduct back within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`

-- Example C (pdf 25-27). C-1: wholly foreign; effect on US import commerce in finished goods,
-- proximately caused, substantial, foreseeable to a reasonable person (the conspirators'
-- unawareness has no field, and the encoding reads foreseeability objectively).
#ASSERT `3: the commerce the conduct involves` `ind wholly foreign` EQUALS `wholly foreign commerce`
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST `ind import, DSRF`) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `a circumstance chapter 3 describes as a sufficient connection: if the agencies so determine, they generally will proceed in the normal course, subject to the considerations of chapter 4 and principles of prosecutorial discretion`
-- C-2: effect found not proximately caused.
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not proceed: the FTAIA precludes the claim on the merits or strips the court of jurisdiction, and courts of appeals differ on which without affecting the agencies' decision`
-- C-3: no effect on US import commerce.
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind wholly foreign` EMPTY `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not proceed: the FTAIA precludes the claim on the merits or strips the court of jurisdiction, and courts of appeals differ on which without affecting the agencies' decision`

-- Example D (pdf 27-28): effect on US interstate commerce, found DSRF ("appears to be").
#ASSERT `3: what the agencies do` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST `ind domestic, DSRF`) `ind equitable` EQUALS JUST `a circumstance chapter 3 describes as a sufficient connection: if the agencies so determine, they generally will proceed in the normal course, subject to the considerations of chapter 4 and principles of prosecutorial discretion`

-- N5a (pdf 28): private plaintiff injured through the effect on US import commerce: may recover.
#ASSERT `3.2: what the text says of a private damages claim` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE))) `ind private` EQUALS JUST `the plaintiff may recover damages for that injury`
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE))) `ind private` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception brings the conduct back within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N5a: foreign injury independent of, not caused by, the US effect: cannot recover.
#ASSERT `3.2: what the text says of a private damages claim` `ind wholly foreign` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))) `ind private, foreign injury` EQUALS JUST `the plaintiff cannot recover damages under the U.S. antitrust laws`
-- N5b: effect not adverse, private damages: does not give rise.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) `ind private` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- N5c: the United States under s.4A, effect found not to have caused its injury: does not give rise.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE)) `ind 4A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE)) `ind 4A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- N5d: the sovereign's equitable or criminal claim: DSRF gives rise, no injury causation needed.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` `ind import, DSRF` `ind equitable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` `ind import, DSRF` `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- N5e: the same conduct, within reach for the prosecution and not for the independent foreign injury.
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception brings the conduct back within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
#ASSERT `3.2: the effects exception` (LIST (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))) `ind private, foreign injury` EQUALS JUST `the effects exception does not bring the conduct within the reach of the Sherman Act and the FTC Act for this claim`
-- N5f: sovereign claim, effect found not adverse: text silent; accept NOTHING or gives rise, reject "does not".
#ASSERT NOT (`3.2: the effect gives rise to the claim` (`ind effect` `U.S. import trade or commerce` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING) `ind criminal` EQUALS JUST FALSE)

-- n.100 (pdf 29): restitution.
#ASSERT `n.100: restitution to a victim` (`Victim of an offense reported under the leniency policy (n.100)` WITH `the victim's antitrust injury is proximately caused by an adverse effect on trade or commerce within the United States, import trade or commerce, or the export trade or commerce of a person engaged in such trade or commerce in the United States` IS FALSE, `that effect was proximately caused by the anticompetitive activity being reported` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Department construes the leniency policy not to require restitution to this victim`
#ASSERT `n.100: restitution to a victim` (`Victim of an offense reported under the leniency policy (n.100)` WITH `the victim's antitrust injury is proximately caused by an adverse effect on trade or commerce within the United States, import trade or commerce, or the export trade or commerce of a person engaged in such trade or commerce in the United States` IS TRUE, `that effect was proximately caused by the anticompetitive activity being reported` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the leniency policy requires applicants to make restitution to the victims of their offense`

§§ `E. Section 3.3 US government financing or purchasing (pdf 29-30)`

-- I build the record with "the substantial portion" as a BOOLEAN: FALSE stands for "not found"
-- (the record has no "unknown").
GIVEN pu IS A BOOLEAN
      iv IS A `U.S. government involvement in a transaction (3.3)`
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
      tx IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of U.S. government financing or purchasing (3.3)`
`ind financing` pu iv sp tx MEANS `Facts of U.S. government financing or purchasing (3.3)` WITH
    `the U.S. government is a purchaser, or substantially funds the purchase, of goods or services for consumption or use abroad` IS pu
    `the involvement` IS iv
    `as a result of its payment or financing, the U.S. government bears a substantial portion of the cost of the transaction` IS sp
    `the effect of the conduct with respect to the sale of the goods or services falls primarily on U.S. taxpayers` IS tx

-- G1, G3: purchaser and substantial portion: "may, in appropriate cases".
#ASSERT `3.3: what the agencies may do` (`ind financing` TRUE `an actual purchase of goods by the U.S. government for shipment abroad` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may, in appropriate cases, take enforcement action`
#ASSERT `3.3: U.S. government interests` (`ind financing` TRUE `another form of U.S. government involvement` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies consider U.S. government interests to be sufficiently affected`
-- G1: effect primarily on taxpayers: "may qualify".
#ASSERT `3.3: whether the case may qualify for redress` (`ind financing` TRUE `an actual purchase of goods by the U.S. government for shipment abroad` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the case may qualify for redress under the federal antitrust laws`
-- G4, G5: international agency, non-earmarked aid: not sufficiently implicated.
#ASSERT `3.3: U.S. government interests` (`ind financing` TRUE `funding of the transaction merely by an international agency` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `U.S. government interests would not be considered to be sufficiently implicated`
#ASSERT `3.3: U.S. government interests` (`ind financing` TRUE `non-earmarked funds received by the foreign government from the United States as part of a general government-to-government aid program` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `U.S. government interests would not be considered to be sufficiently implicated`
-- G6: earmarked loan on ordinary terms ("another form"), no substantial-portion finding: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `3.3: U.S. government interests` (`ind financing` TRUE `another form of U.S. government involvement` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `F. Section 4.1 comity (pdf 30-32)`

-- CO1, CO3, CO6: every listed consideration is reported, and no outcome is computed.
#ASSERT `4.1: the comity considerations that are present` (`Comity facts (4.1)` WITH `significant interests of a foreign sovereign would be affected` IS TRUE, `there is a purpose to affect, or an actual effect on, U.S. commerce` IS TRUE, `the effects of the conduct on the United States are significant and foreseeable` IS TRUE, `enforcement would conflict with a foreign jurisdiction's law or articulated policy` IS TRUE, `the enforcement activities of another jurisdiction, including their remedies, may be affected` IS TRUE, `the objectives sought by U.S. enforcement could be achieved by foreign enforcement` IS TRUE, `a foreign sovereign encourages or discourages the course of conduct, or leaves parties free to choose among courses of conduct` IS TRUE) EQUALS LIST `whether significant interests of any foreign sovereign would be affected`, `the existence of a purpose to affect or an actual effect on U.S. commerce`, `the significance and foreseeability of the effects of the anticompetitive conduct on the United States`, `the degree of conflict with a foreign jurisdiction's law or articulated policy`, `the extent to which the enforcement activities of another jurisdiction, including remedies resulting from those enforcement activities, may be affected`, `the effectiveness of foreign enforcement as compared to U.S. enforcement`, `the extent to which a foreign sovereign encourages or discourages certain courses of conduct or leaves parties free to choose among different courses of conduct`
-- CO4: a foreign authority's action does not preclude; the Agency will determine.
#ASSERT `4.1: what a foreign authority's investigation or action does, if there is one` TRUE EQUALS JUST `it will not preclude an investigation or enforcement action by either the Department or the Commission: the Agency will determine whether, in light of the foreign authority's actions, investigation or enforcement is warranted, and may coordinate with that authority`

GIVEN cb IS A BOOLEAN
      nu IS A BOOLEAN
      bs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Foreign law and the conduct (4.1)`
`ind foreign law` cb nu bs MEANS `Foreign law and the conduct (4.1)` WITH
    `a person subject to the laws of both sovereigns can comply with both` IS cb
    `the foreign law is neutral as to the conduct` IS nu
    `the only foreign law said to conflict is a blocking statute, shown by nothing more than its existence` IS bs

-- CO5a, b, c, d.
#ASSERT `4.1: whether a conflict of law exists` (`ind foreign law` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no conflict of law exists, because a person subject to the laws of both sovereigns can comply with both`
#ASSERT `4.1: whether a conflict of law exists` (`ind foreign law` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `no conflict exists, because the foreign law is neutral as to the conduct`
#ASSERT `4.1: whether a conflict of law exists` (`ind foreign law` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the agencies do not view the mere existence of a blocking statute as creating a conflict of law for purposes of the comity analysis`
#ASSERT `4.1: whether a conflict of law exists` (`ind foreign law` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `a conflict of law exists, and comity may counsel in favor of declining enforcement`

§§ `G. Section 4.2.1 foreign sovereign immunity (pdf 32-35)`

GIVEN kd IS A `Kind of entity (4.2.1)`
      sl IS A BOOLEAN
      og IS A BOOLEAN
      mj IS A BOOLEAN
      tc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Entity before the FSIA (4.2.1)`
`ind entity` kd sl og mj tc MEANS `Entity before the FSIA (4.2.1)` WITH
    `the kind of entity` IS kd
    `it is a separate legal person, corporate or otherwise` IS sl
    `it is an organ of a foreign state or political subdivision of one` IS og
    `a majority of its shares or other ownership interest is owned by the foreign state itself or a political subdivision of it` IS mj
    `it is a citizen of a State of the United States, or created under the laws of a third country` IS tc

GIVEN cv IS A BOOLEAN
      pp IS A BOOLEAN
      gp IS A BOOLEAN
      l1 IS A BOOLEAN
      l2 IS A BOOLEAN
      l3 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Action against a foreign state (4.2.1)`
`ind action` cv pp gp l1 l2 l3 MEANS `Action against a foreign state (4.2.1)` WITH
    `the action is a civil case` IS cv
    `in the activity, the foreign state acts in the manner of a private player within a market, not as a regulator of it` IS pp
    `the activity has a public or governmental purpose` IS gp
    `the action is based upon the activity carried on in the United States by the foreign state, with substantial contact with the United States` IS l1
    `the action is based upon an act performed in the United States in connection with the activity of the foreign state elsewhere` IS l2
    `the action is based upon an act outside the territory of the United States in connection with the activity of the foreign state elsewhere, and that act causes a direct effect in the United States` IS l3

`ind the state` MEANS `ind entity` `a foreign state itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- F1a, F2 limb 1: commercial activity in the US: not immune.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` `ind the state` (`ind action` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the foreign state is not immune from the jurisdiction of U.S. courts: the commercial activity exception`
-- F2 limb 3 with a direct effect: not immune.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` `ind the state` (`ind action` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the foreign state is not immune from the jurisdiction of U.S. courts: the commercial activity exception`
-- F2a: commercial activity elsewhere, act abroad without direct effect in the US (no limb): shielded.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` `ind the state` (`ind action` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the FSIA shields the foreign state from the civil jurisdiction of U.S. courts, subject to its other enumerated exceptions and to treaties in place at the time of its enactment`
-- F2b, F3: regulator, not private player, even with a US-based activity: exception does not apply.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` `ind the state` (`ind action` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the FSIA shields the foreign state from the civil jurisdiction of U.S. courts, subject to its other enumerated exceptions and to treaties in place at the time of its enactment`
-- F3: nature, not purpose: a private-player activity with a public purpose is commercial.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the activity is commercial` (`ind action` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- F1c: criminal case: text silent on the FSIA: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` `ind the state` (`ind action` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- F4a: state-owned corporation, majority held by the state itself: a foreign state.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the entity is a foreign state under the FSIA` (`ind entity` `another entity, which may be an agency or instrumentality of a foreign state` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- F4b: created under the laws of a third country: my frozen answer "not an agency or
-- instrumentality", so not a foreign state. The encoding returns NOTHING (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the entity is a foreign state under the FSIA` (`ind entity` `another entity, which may be an agency or instrumentality of a foreign state` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- F4c: majority held only indirectly (field FALSE), not an organ: my frozen answer "not covered
-- by the majority-ownership prong" (Dole Food). The encoding returns NOTHING (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the entity is a foreign state under the FSIA` (`ind entity` `another entity, which may be an agency or instrumentality of a foreign state` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- F4d: individual foreign official: FSIA does not apply.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: foreign sovereign immunity` (`ind entity` `an individual foreign official` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`ind action` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the FSIA does not apply: the immunity of an individual foreign official is governed by the common law`
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the entity is a foreign state under the FSIA` (`ind entity` `an individual foreign official` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- F5: a state-owned enterprise in the commercial marketplace: same as private foreign firms.
#ASSERT `4.2.1: the commercial activities of a state-owned enterprise` (`ind entity` `another entity, which may be an agency or instrumentality of a foreign state` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) (`ind action` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the commercial activities of the enterprise are subject to the U.S. antitrust laws to the same extent as the activities of privately owned foreign firms`

§§ `H. Section 4.2.2 foreign sovereign compulsion (pdf 35-37)`

GIVEN ms IS A `Foreign government measure (4.2.2)`
      di IS A BOOLEAN
      cb IS A BOOLEAN
      pl IS A `Place of the compelled conduct (4.2.2)`
      gv IS A BOOLEAN
      fc IS A BOOLEAN
      la IS A BOOLEAN
      sg IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of foreign sovereign compulsion (4.2.2)`
`ind compulsion` ms di cb pl gv fc la sg MEANS `Facts of foreign sovereign compulsion (4.2.2)` WITH
    `the measure` IS ms
    `the conduct is discretionary` IS di
    `the party can comply with both the foreign law and the U.S. antitrust laws` IS cb
    `where the compelled conduct is accomplished` IS pl
    `the order comes from the foreign government acting in its governmental capacity` IS gv
    `the conduct would fall within the FSIA commercial activity exception` IS fc
    `the conduct is lawful, approved, or encouraged in the foreign jurisdiction` IS la
    `the foreign jurisdiction has a strong policy in favor of the conduct` IS sg

`ind command` MEANS `a command, refusal to comply with which would give rise to the imposition of penal or other severe sanctions`
`ind recognised` MEANS JUST `the criteria are satisfied: the agencies would acknowledge a defense of sovereign compulsion`
`ind not recognised` MEANS JUST `the criteria are not satisfied: the agencies will not refrain from an enforcement action based on considerations of foreign sovereign compulsion, and would also consider whether comity factors counsel against one`

-- Example E, Gamma (pdf 37): ordered cutbacks with substantial penalties, production in Gamma,
-- governmental capacity: the agencies "would acknowledge a defense".
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE FALSE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `ind recognised`
-- Example E, Alpha and Beta: urged, not required; the producers agreed among themselves (I set
-- "discretionary" TRUE and "can comply with both" TRUE, since nothing required the cutbacks).
-- No compulsion defence; the result names comity too (n.127).
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `a measure short of compulsion` TRUE TRUE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
-- CP1: possible to comply with both: no legal excuse.
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE TRUE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
-- CP2: lawful, encouraged and strongly favoured abroad, but no command: no bar.
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `no measure of the foreign government` FALSE FALSE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
-- CP3: discretionary conduct: outside the defence.
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` TRUE FALSE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
-- CP4c: compelled conduct in the US (US subsidiaries made to cartelise): "will not recognize".
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE FALSE `in the United States` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
-- CP4d: third country: accept "not recognised" or NOTHING; reject "recognised".
#ASSERT NOT (`4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE FALSE `not entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory, and not in the United States` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind recognised`)
-- CP4e: order in a commercial capacity: no defence (both spellings of it).
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE FALSE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`
#ASSERT `4.2.2: foreign sovereign compulsion` (`ind compulsion` `ind command` FALSE FALSE `entirely within the foreign sovereign's own territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind not recognised`

GIVEN fm IS A BOOLEAN
      dt IS A BOOLEAN
      uq IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Formal representation of compulsion (4.2.2)`
`ind representation` fm dt uq MEANS `Formal representation of compulsion (4.2.2)` WITH
    `the foreign government has formally represented that refusal to comply with its command would give rise to penal or other severe sanctions` IS fm
    `the representation contains enough detail to enable the agencies to see precisely how the compulsion would be accomplished under foreign law` IS dt
    `the statement is unsupported or ambiguous, or appears on its face to be internally inconsistent` IS uq

-- CP5: detailed formal representation: generally sufficient.
#ASSERT `4.2.2: how the agencies regard the representation` (`ind representation` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as a general matter, the agencies regard the representation as sufficient to establish that the conduct has been compelled`
-- CP5: lacking detail: not established (accept NOTHING too); reject "sufficient".
#ASSERT NOT (`4.2.2: how the agencies regard the representation` (`ind representation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `as a general matter, the agencies regard the representation as sufficient to establish that the conduct has been compelled`)
-- CP5: detailed but internally inconsistent: may not be dispositive; reject "sufficient".
#ASSERT NOT (`4.2.2: how the agencies regard the representation` (`ind representation` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `as a general matter, the agencies regard the representation as sufficient to establish that the conduct has been compelled`)

§§ `I. Section 4.2.3 act of state (pdf 38-39)`

GIVEN ac IS A `Actor of the conduct complained of (4.2.3)`
      pa IS A BOOLEAN
      wt IS A BOOLEAN
      gm IS A BOOLEAN
      ap IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of an act of state (4.2.3)`
`ind act` ac pa wt gm ap MEANS `Facts of an act of state (4.2.3)` WITH
    `the actor` IS ac
    `the specific conduct complained of is a public act of the sovereign` IS pa
    `the act was taken within the territorial jurisdiction of the sovereign` IS wt
    `the conduct relates to a matter that is governmental, rather than commercial` IS gm
    `the foreign government approved or condoned the acts` IS ap

-- AS1, AS2.
#ASSERT `4.2.3: act of state` (`ind act` `an individual government official acting outside the official capacity` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the doctrine does not apply to the acts of individual government officials acting outside their official capacity`
#ASSERT `4.2.3: act of state` (`ind act` `a private actor` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the doctrine does not apply to private actors, even when their acts are approved or condoned by the foreign government`
-- AS3a: a licence granted by the sovereign, in its territory, governmental: "may decline".
#ASSERT `4.2.3: act of state` (`ind act` `the foreign sovereign` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may exercise enforcement discretion and decline to challenge the foreign act of state`
-- AS3b: commercial: discretion not triggered; accept NOTHING; reject "may decline".
#ASSERT NOT (`4.2.3: act of state` (`ind act` `the foreign sovereign` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may exercise enforcement discretion and decline to challenge the foreign act of state`)

§§ `J. Section 4.2.4 petitioning of sovereigns (pdf 39-40)`

GIVEN en IS A `Government entity petitioned (4.2.4)`
      ef IS A BOOLEAN
      sh IS A BOOLEAN
      na IS A BOOLEAN
      it IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of petitioning (4.2.4)`
`ind petition` en ef sh na it MEANS `Facts of petitioning (4.2.4)` WITH
    `the government entity petitioned` IS en
    `the conduct is an effort to obtain or influence action by the government entity` IS ef
    `the petitioning, ostensibly directed toward influencing governmental action, is a mere sham to cover an attempt to interfere directly with the business relationships of a competitor` IS sh
    `Noerr-Pennington would otherwise not apply` IS na
    `the intent or effect of the effort is to restrain or monopolize trade` IS it

-- Example F, PT1 (pdf 39-40): genuine complaint to Alpha's Ministry of Mines, aimed at a
-- monopoly: no enforcement action.
#ASSERT `4.2.4: petitioning of sovereigns` (`ind petition` `a foreign government entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not challenge under the antitrust laws the genuine effort to obtain or influence action by the foreign government entity`
-- PT2: sham: the discretion is not exercised (not "will challenge").
#ASSERT `4.2.4: petitioning of sovereigns` (`ind petition` `a foreign government entity` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not exercise this discretion: the petitioning is a sham`
-- PT3: Noerr-Pennington would otherwise not apply.
#ASSERT `4.2.4: petitioning of sovereigns` (`ind petition` `a foreign government entity` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not exercise this discretion: Noerr-Pennington would otherwise not apply`

§§ `K. Chapter 5 cooperation (pdf 40-54)`

-- K1 (5, n.138, pdf 41).
#ASSERT `5: cooperation with the foreign authority` `the Agency and the foreign authority are conducting parallel investigations of the matter` EQUALS `the Agency may consult with the relevant foreign authorities about the matter, and coordinate and cooperate with those authorities conducting parallel investigations`
#ASSERT `5: cooperation with the foreign authority` `the Agency or the foreign authority has closed its investigation, after they cooperated` EQUALS `an Agency may continue that cooperation when either it or the foreign authority has closed its investigation`
#ASSERT `5: cooperation with the foreign authority` `only one of them has an open investigation of the matter` EQUALS `the agencies may engage in general discussions with foreign authorities on matters in which only one authority has an open investigation`

GIVEN pc IS A BOOLEAN
      pv IS A BOOLEAN
      ab IS A BOOLEAN
      bl IS A BOOLEAN
      sr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Documents or information sought (5.1.1)`
`ind documents` pc pv ab bl sr MEANS `Documents or information sought (5.1.1)` WITH
    `they are within the possession, custody, or control of an individual or entity subject to the jurisdiction of the United States` IS pc
    `they are protected by the attorney-client privilege or the work-product doctrine` IS pv
    `they are located outside the United States` IS ab
    `a foreign statute purports to prevent disclosing them for use in U.S. proceedings` IS bl
    `they are sought by a Second Request in a transaction notified under the HSR Act` IS sr

-- K4 (5.1.1, pdf 42): documents abroad, controlled by a person subject to US jurisdiction, not
-- privileged: may compel.
#ASSERT `5.1.1: whether the agencies may compel production` (`ind documents` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may compel the production of the documents or information, including documents or information located outside the United States`
-- K4a: privileged: my frozen answer "cannot compel". The encoding has no value for it and
-- returns NOTHING (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT (NOT (`5.1.1: whether the agencies may compel production` (`ind documents` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING)) AND (NOT (`5.1.1: whether the agencies may compel production` (`ind documents` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may compel the production of the documents or information, including documents or information located outside the United States`))
-- K4b: holder not subject to US jurisdiction: my frozen answer "no compulsory authority". Same
-- shape (expected to FAIL).
#ASSERT (NOT (`5.1.1: whether the agencies may compel production` (`ind documents` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING)) AND (NOT (`5.1.1: whether the agencies may compel production` (`ind documents` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may compel the production of the documents or information, including documents or information located outside the United States`))
-- K5: Second Request, no matter where located.
#ASSERT `5.1.1: what compliance with a Second Request requires` (`ind documents` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `compliance with a Second Request requires production of all responsive documents and information, no matter where located`
-- K6: a blocking statute does not excuse noncompliance.
#ASSERT `5.1.1: what the mere existence of a blocking statute does` (`ind documents` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the mere existence of the foreign statute does not excuse noncompliance with a request for documents or information from one of the agencies`

GIVEN ki IS A `Kind of information (5.1.4, 5.2)`
      wv IS A `Waiver of confidentiality (5.1.4)`
      ud IS A BOOLEAN
      hs IS A BOOLEAN
      ia IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Information for a foreign authority (5.1.4)`
`ind info` ki wv ud hs ia MEANS `Information for a foreign authority (5.1.4)` WITH
    `the kind of information` IS ki
    `the foreign authority is also investigating the transaction or conduct` IS TRUE
    `the information was submitted pursuant to the HSR Act` IS hs
    `the waiver` IS wv
    `the agencies have reached an understanding that the foreign authority will maintain the information in confidence, consistent with its laws and rules` IS ud
    `an IAEAA mutual assistance agreement is in force between the United States and the foreign authority` IS ia

`ind covering waiver` MEANS `the person has granted a waiver for this matter that designates the foreign authority`
`ind no waiver` MEANS `no waiver has been requested or granted`
`ind prohibited` MEANS JUST `confidentiality obligations generally prohibit the agencies from disclosing to foreign authorities confidential information submitted by a person`

-- K17: public information: may share.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `relevant publicly available information` `ind no waiver` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may share relevant publicly available information with the foreign authority`
-- K18a, K18b: agency non-public information.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `agency non-public information` `ind no waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `it remains in the agencies' discretion whether to share agency non-public information with the cooperating foreign authority`
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `agency non-public information` `ind no waiver` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `not before the agencies have reached an understanding that the foreign authority will maintain the agency non-public information in confidence and in accordance with its laws and rules`
-- K19a: confidential, no waiver, no IAEAA: generally prohibited.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind no waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind prohibited`
-- K19b and Example G, Alpha (pdf 49): waiver for the matter naming the authority, understanding: will provide.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind covering waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will provide the information to the foreign authority pursuant to the waiver`
-- K20: waiver not for this matter or not naming this authority: does not cover.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `the person has granted a waiver, but not for this matter or not designating the foreign authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind prohibited`
-- K21: covering waiver, no understanding: accept "not provided" or NOTHING; reject "provided".
#ASSERT NOT (`5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind covering waiver` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will provide the information to the foreign authority pursuant to the waiver`)
-- A5 (2.6, 5.1.3): IAEAA route for non-HSR evidence; not for HSR materials.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind no waiver` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `under an IAEAA agreement, the agencies may share evidence relating to antitrust violations already in their possession, including statutorily protected confidential information, subject to certain limitations`
#ASSERT NOT (`5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind no waiver` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST `under an IAEAA agreement, the agencies may share evidence relating to antitrust violations already in their possession, including statutorily protected confidential information, subject to certain limitations`)
-- K23: declining a waiver does not preclude sharing public or agency non-public information,
-- and does not prejudice the outcome.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `agency non-public information` `the person has declined to provide a waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `it remains in the agencies' discretion whether to share agency non-public information with the cooperating foreign authority`
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `relevant publicly available information` `the person has declined to provide a waiver` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may share relevant publicly available information with the foreign authority`
#ASSERT `5.1.4: what refusing a waiver does to the investigation` `the person has declined to provide a waiver` EQUALS JUST `refusal to provide a waiver will not prejudice the outcome of an investigation, though in some cases the absence of a waiver may have practical effects such as increasing the risk of inconsistent outcomes between jurisdictions`
-- Example G, Delta and Epsilon (pdf 49): no waivers; no confidential business information exchanged.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: sharing the information with the foreign authority` (`ind info` `confidential information submitted by a person` `ind no waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `ind prohibited`
-- K22.
#ASSERT `5.1.4: what the agencies say of information from a foreign authority` (`Information from a foreign authority (5.1.4)` WITH `it is privileged under U.S. law` IS TRUE, `the agencies received it from the foreign authority pursuant to a waiver` IS FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the agencies will not seek information that is privileged under U.S. law from foreign authorities through waivers or other cooperative activities`
#ASSERT `5.1.4: what the agencies say of information from a foreign authority` (`Information from a foreign authority (5.1.4)` WITH `it is privileged under U.S. law` IS FALSE, `the agencies received it from the foreign authority pursuant to a waiver` IS TRUE) EQUALS LIST `the agencies will protect information received from a foreign authority pursuant to a waiver under applicable provisions of U.S. law`

-- K24 (5.1.5, pdf 50): remedy reaching abroad only to the extent needed and consistent with comity.
#ASSERT `5.1.5: a remedy that includes conduct or assets outside the United States` (`Remedy reaching outside the United States (5.1.5)` WITH `including them is needed to effectively redress harm or threatened harm to U.S. commerce and consumers` IS TRUE, `including them is consistent with the Agency's international comity analysis` IS TRUE) EQUALS `including the conduct or assets outside the United States is within the extent to which an Agency will seek such a remedy`
#ASSERT `5.1.5: a remedy that includes conduct or assets outside the United States` (`Remedy reaching outside the United States (5.1.5)` WITH `including them is needed to effectively redress harm or threatened harm to U.S. commerce and consumers` IS FALSE, `including them is consistent with the Agency's international comity analysis` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Agency will not seek to include the conduct or assets outside the United States: including them is not needed to effectively redress harm or threatened harm to U.S. commerce and consumers`
#ASSERT `5.1.5: a remedy that includes conduct or assets outside the United States` (`Remedy reaching outside the United States (5.1.5)` WITH `including them is needed to effectively redress harm or threatened harm to U.S. commerce and consumers` IS TRUE, `including them is consistent with the Agency's international comity analysis` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Agency will not seek to include the conduct or assets outside the United States: including them is not consistent with the Agency's international comity analysis`

GIVEN ki IS A `Kind of information (5.1.4, 5.2)`
      pd IS A `Person disclosing (5.2)`
      ex IS A BOOLEAN
      wv IS A `Waiver of confidentiality (5.1.4)`
GIVETH A `Criminal investigation information for a foreign authority (5.2)`
`ind criminal info` ki pd ex wv MEANS `Criminal investigation information for a foreign authority (5.2)` WITH
    `the kind of information` IS ki
    `the person disclosing` IS pd
    `an exception to the grand jury secrecy rule applies` IS ex
    `the waiver` IS wv

`ind grand jury prohibited` MEANS JUST `the Department is prohibited from disclosing matters occurring before the grand jury absent an applicable exception, and the prohibition cannot be waived by a subject of the investigation, a grand jury witness, or a recipient of a grand jury subpoena`

